<!-- Entry for hk-modding/modlinks, the database Lumafly reads.

     Easiest route (recommended by the maintainers):
       1. Open https://github.com/hk-modding/modlinks/blob/main/ModLinks.xml
       2. Click the pencil icon, paste this block in alphabetical order by <Name>
       3. "Commit Changes" -> "Propose Changes"; GitHub makes the fork, branch and PR for you

     <Name> is the folder the mod is installed into, so it must match the DLL name and must not
     contain spaces. The release zip has its files at the root - the installer creates the folder.

     The SHA256 must match the release asset exactly or CI fails and Lumafly refuses the download.
     After any new release:
       shasum -a 256 dist/HalallowKnight-<version>.zip | awk '{print toupper($1)}'
     then open another PR updating <Version> and SHA256.
-->
